        <headline>AOG - BLEED TRIP RTO</headline>
        <description>TSRV AOG SUPPORT - RH BLEED TRIP 

BACKGROUND: DATUM A/C IS CURRENTLY AOG IN LBA DUE TO RH BLEED TRIP RTO.  THIS WORK ORDER HAS BEEN RAISED TO PERFORM BLEED HEALTH ON THE RH BLEED SYSTEM.
 
ACTION:  
 
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.      

* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM        

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.

3. LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:         

A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE. 

B) CONTROL PRESSURE SENSE LINE TO PRSOV. 

C) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR. 

D) 390 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION. E). SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV.   

4. INSPECT THE BAR HARNESS FOR PATH TO GROUND ON PINS 9 + 10 OF DP1102 OF BLEED AIR REGULATOR - IF CONTINUITY FOUND REFERENCE WDM 36-11-11 BLEED AIR VALVE CONTROL TO ISOLATE S20 OVERTEMP SWITCH. IF NIL FAULT CONTINUE TO STEP 6.
 
5. CHECK FOR CONTINUITY THROUGH BLEED AIR REGULATOR 220 PRESSURE SWITCH AT PINS 9 AND 10 OF BLEED AIR REGULATOR M1180 - IF CONTINUITY IS FOUND REPLACE BLEED AIR REGULATOR IAW AMM 36-11-03/401 BLEED AIR REGULATOR - REMOVAL/INSTALLATION.

6. IF TROUBLESHOOTING IS INDETERMINATE DUE TO THE INTERMITTENT NATURE: 

-  REPLACE THE RH BAR HARNESS (MW0311) IAW AMM 73-21-06/401.

7. IF MW0311 HARNESS WAS REPLACED, ENSURE TO PERFORM FFCC VIBRATION SENSOR TEST (AVM SYSTEM OPERATIONAL TEST) PER AMM 77-31-00-710-801-F00. 

NOTE: THIS STEP REQUIRES THE AFFECTED ENGINE TO BE OPERATED AT 70% N1 FOR 2 MINUTES.

8. RETURN AC TO SERVICE WITH ALL FINDINGS FROM THIS WO DOCUMENTED AND CLOSED EITHER THROUGH POSITIVE MAINTENANCE ACTION OR AN ACCEPTABLE DEFERRAL.   

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.     

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
